  "conclusion": "Joint pose/focal optimization reduces the optimized objective and image residual in these tests, but worsens both raw and similarity-aligned 3D accuracy. A lower optimization cost does not establish calibration or reconstruction accuracy. Fixed calibrated cameras remain the sensible default.",
  "limitations": [
    "Single synthetic seed, analytic trajectories, controlled low input calibration errors; not a paper benchmark or real-world validation.",
    "Motion prior and camera parameters are jointly adjustable; the observed calibration drift can reduce motion cost. This experiment identifies the behavior but does not prove a unique causal mechanism.",
    "Raw world-coordinate camera errors are not post-hoc aligned; point metrics include separately reported Sim(3)-aligned errors."
  ]
